Vikram and Betal: The Helpful Child (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100140

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a child who always helped others,” said Betal. “He was kind to everyone in his village.”

One day, he saw an old woman struggling to carry a basket.

The child quickly went and helped her.

The old woman blessed him and said, “Your kindness will always bring you happiness.”

Later, the child found a lost purse on the road.

He remembered the old woman’s words.

He returned the purse to its owner.

The owner was very happy and rewarded the child.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the child special?”

Vikram replied, “His kindness and honesty made him special.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Kindness and honesty make a person great.
